Z||000006||sastian||04-02-2001||07:44 PM||||ok well im getting her to "pop" radomly but not start. Im sure of the firing order. but i cant verify wich is "cylinder 1" on the cap!!! any help?????||||reg||1
Z||000007||JohnnyK||04-02-2001||08:12 PM||||Umm.. i don't know why these guys haven't mentioned it, but if the distributor was out, you need to find top dead center of cylinder number 1.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Mark||04-02-2001||09:19 PM||||Follow the spark plug wire from #1 plug (rear bank, passanger side) to the cap.  Also, given the effort required to change plugs, I would put new ones in.||||reg||1
Z||000009||rogergarrison||04-02-2001||09:28 PM||||he didnt have it out, just worked around because of a loose bolt.||||reg||1
Z||000010||sastian||04-02-2001||11:38 PM||||well after a lot of reading i decided to pull the No. 1 plug. ( changed them all while I was at it. bonnet off and all) Then i had my wife tap the ignition while i felt for the compression stoke with the cap off. I kept noticing the compression blow when the rotor faced the 10'oclock. I was expecting to see it at the 2 from what i have read. but after repeated observation i decided to start the No. 1 wire near te 10 o'clock. buttoned the cap on, replaced the plug and started clockwise from the top right corner. turned the key, she cleared her throat and fired right up.  I dont know if that where its supposed to be but it works now. i'll tune it out tomorrow. I need to paint the timing marks and i tought that doing from underneath would be better since ill be changing the oil on her tomorrow night. But you guys ( and this discussion board) really helped! any thing you want to make sure i do while i tune it tomorrow?||||reg||1
